OSKit INET Server — Internet Sockets
====================================

Minix 3-style socket server. Fronts the NIC driver (virtio-net)
with an ARP cache + IPv4 stack + UDP + TCP (Reno + SACK) +
ICMP echo. Loopback (127.0.0.1) is served from per-socket queues
without touching the NIC; everything else goes through
`inet_nic_send_packet` / the RX subscription.

Protocol surface
----------------

UDP + raw-ish ops:
- SOCKET (1), BIND (2), SENDTO (3), RECVFROM (4), CLOSE (5)
- RECVFROM_TIMEOUT (18) — used for both timed recv and the
  O_NONBLOCK path (timeout_ms=0 ⇒ immediate EAGAIN via status=1)
- ARP_PROBE (19) — RFC 5227 conflict detection, driven by dhclient
- ICMP_SEND (21) / ICMP_CHECK (22) — ping utility
- SET_IP_CONFIG (16) / GET_IP_CONFIG (17) — driven by dhclient

TCP:
- TCP_CONNECT (10), TCP_SEND (11), TCP_RECV (12), TCP_CLOSE (13),
  TCP_LISTEN (14), TCP_ACCEPT (15)
- TCP_DEBUG (20) — internal state dump for test harness
- TCP_RECV_NB (26) — non-blocking recv returning -EAGAIN (-11)
- TCP_SHUTDOWN (27) — SHUT_WR emits FIN without parking caller
- TCP_GETNAME (25) / UDP_GETNAME (24) — sockaddr_in for
  getsockname / getpeername

Housekeeping:
- PID_EXIT (23) — PM-driven cleanup of sockets whose owner_tid
  matches a terminated thread

All multi-byte integers are big-endian. Each request has a
1-byte command code in `buf[0]`; replies start with a 1-byte
status (0 on success, -errno on failure, -1 for opaque error).
Handlers enforce per-fd ownership: `owner_tid == sender` is
required alongside in-use, so process A can't issue ops on
process B's sockets.

    module oskit.servers

    import oskit.ipc.{port_create, port_register, ipc_recv_notify, ipc_reply}
    import oskit.services.{rs_ready, notify_read_self, svc_timer_subscribe, monotonic_ms}
    import std.net.{AF_INET, SOCK_DGRAM, INADDR_ANY, INADDR_LOOPBACK, ipv4, ipv4_octet,
        ETHERTYPE_IPV4, ETHERTYPE_ARP, ARP_OP_REQUEST, ARP_OP_REPLY,
        IP_PROTO_ICMP, IP_PROTO_UDP, IP_PROTO_TCP, ICMP_ECHO_REQ, ICMP_ECHO_REP,
        ICMP_DEST_UNREACH, ICMP_CODE_FRAG_NEEDED,
        pkt_read_u16, pkt_match_ipv4, net_checksum}


Protocol command codes (byte value of buf[0]).

    const INET_CMD_SOCKET       = 1
    const INET_CMD_BIND         = 2
